[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The render reads an export generated from the held graph

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-EXPORT-PAYLOAD
TITLE: The render reads an export generated from the held graph
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
A render obtains the export JSON from the held graph rather than by running a
fresh export. StrictDoc's JSON generator is a pure function of a built index --
strictdoc's own server calls it against its live one -- so the daemon runs it
against the resident graph into a directory the caller names, and every
downstream consumer reads the same bytes it reads today.

The payload is written to a directory rather than returned, because the current
export is 10.3 MB. An export reconciles first, like any read.

One thing about those bytes did change, deliberately, and it is the only
divergence from a hand-run export. StrictDoc's JSON generator reads exactly
TYPE, FORMAT, VALUE and LINE_RANGE off a File relation, so an element-grained
relation would export as a whole-file one and every consumer would see a
coarser graph than the corpus declares. sdoc_model.carry_file_element_into_json
patches that one generator method in memory before each export -- idempotent,
and fail-closed on an upstream rename -- so the daemon's export carries ELEMENT
and ID too. The patch lives here rather than in the package because
overlays/dev-tools/strictdoc.nix re-exports upstream's derivation unchanged for
cache-hit parity. `strictdoc export` run by hand therefore still drops both
fields, and that asymmetry is the cost.

No downstream code changed. Wireline, view-check, render and status read the
shape they always read, with two more optional keys on a File relation, and
none of them imports strictdoc. The daemon's own graph load passes
skip_source_files=True, so the source-traceability walk the project config
turns on does not run inside it and none of that walk's cost reaches a read.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Updated 2026-09-03 for commits 6fbaa76b and c64a0147: the daemon's export
carries ELEMENT and ID through an in-memory patch, and the daemon's own load
is exempt from the source-traceability walk the project config now enables.
<<<
